Social Security Numbers (SSNs) do not have an expiration date. Once issued, your SSN remains valid for your entire life. 

However, if you are referring to the expiration date on your **passport** or another form of ID for a visa application, the general rule for most countries is that your passport must be valid for at least **six months beyond your intended period of stay**. 

If your passport or travel document expires before that six-month window, it is highly likely that it is too close to the expiration date, and you will need to renew it before applying for your visa. 

